course: dictionary
lesson: 11016
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it, which is the context. The word watershed is a good example: it can mean a line of high land, an area of land that drains into a river, an important turning point, or a time on TV.
explain: «The line of high land between two basins is a watershed.» Here it is a ridge that splits the rain: water on one side flows to one river, and water on the other side flows to another. The clues are line, high land and basins, which tell you it is a place, not a time.
explain: Now look at a different sentence: «Moving to a new school was a watershed in her life.» The clue is life, and the idea of things changing for good. A watershed moment is a turning point. Check by swapping in your meaning: "a turning point in her life" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A watershed is a line of high land, such as a ridge, that divides two areas whose rivers flow in different directions.
fact: In US English, a watershed can be the whole area of land whose water drains into one river or lake.
fact: A watershed moment is an important turning point, when things change.
fact: In the UK, «the watershed» is the time in the evening after which programmes for adults can be shown.
fact: The same word can name a hill, a river area, a turning point or a TV time, so always use the clues to choose.
exercise: «The line of high land between two basins is a watershed.» What is a watershed in this sentence? | *A line of high land that divides two areas whose rivers flow different ways | A time when an adult TV programme starts | A busy shopping street | A place where a river ends in the sea
exercise: Mia says, «Winning the scholarship was a watershed in her life.» What does watershed mean here? | A rainy day in the hills | A ridge on a mountain | The edge of a lake | *A turning point when things change
exercise: Dad says, «Keep the cartoons until after the watershed.» What is the watershed? | *The evening time after which adult TV programmes can be shown | The river that flows into the sea | A line of high land | The start of the school holidays
test: In geography, rain falls on a hill and runs down into one river. What is the whole area of land that sends its water to that river called? | A glacier | A desert | *A watershed | A volcano
test: Which sentence uses watershed to mean a turning point? | «The watershed is the time after which adult programmes can be shown.» | *«Losing her first match was a watershed moment that made her train harder.» | «The river flows east into the sea.»
exam: «Before the watershed, the children watched cartoons.» What does the watershed mean here? | A line of high land between two rivers | A moment when a river changes direction | A wide area of land drained by a lake | *The evening time after which adult TV programmes can be shown
